    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d860">

                <pb facs="0815" n="805" sameAs="frus:frus1941v05/pg805"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.811/1168: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Ambassador in Japan</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Grew</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1941-11-24T23:00:00-05:00">November 24,
                            1941—11 p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>775. Shanghai’s November 7, 10 a.m. to Chungking and Chungking’s 447, November
                    13, 10 a.m. to the Department,<anchor n="47" xml:id="d860-f1"/> Whangpoo
                    Conservancy. The Department desires that you make appropriate representations to
                    the Foreign Office in regard to the recent action of the Japanese naval
                    authorities at Shanghai in chartering the vessel <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Chienshe</hi>. You may state in substance that the American Government
                    considers that the agreement reached in 1939 between the Whangpoo Conservancy
                    Board and the Japanese authorities at Shanghai contains no provisions which
                    would justify or empower the Japanese authorities to take over and use
                    Conservancy equipment; and that this action is an impairment of the integrity of
                    the Whangpoo Conservancy Board and in disregard of the international character
                    and status of that body.<anchor n="48" xml:id="d860-f2"/>
                </p>
                <p>Sent to Tokyo via Shanghai. Repeated to Chungking and Peiping.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d860-f1" n="47" xml:id="d860-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed, but see footnote 42, <ref target="#pg804">p. 804</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d860-f2" n="48" xml:id="d860-f2-content">
                <p>The American and British Embassies in Japan made prompt representations to the
                    Japanese Foreign Office (893.811/1169).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
